  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">New Reacci&#xc3;&#xb3;n-Independent Media Resilience-PSE Addendum (ReMedios)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Central America Regional):  The Independent Media Resilience (ReMedios) activity enhances regional collective action against corruption by improving the tracking of transnational corruption. This will be accomplished by improving the quality and quantity of collaboration among independent journalists to produce data-driven investigations. Interventions will focus on strengthening the leadership, organizational resilience, and management of key partners, ensuring successful knowledge transfer. Key to these efforts is the development of the Central American Journalist Network, a new regional consortium that will promote the sustainability of efforts by providing technical resources, collaboration tools, and protection to journalists. Through the network, USAID will provide technical assistance, skill-building, and security services to support journalism focused on institutional reform, enhancing governance, and making policies transparent. The primary implementing partner is a media support NGO working in over 100 countries that trains journalists, advances internet freedom, and helps media outlets become financially sustainable.With FY 2024 funds, USAID will expand regional legal assistance, protection networks, risk management strategies, and digital security for anti-corruption activists, whistleblowers, and journalists. The activity will deliver technical assistance and skill-building through subgrants and cross-border reporting. USAID will promote a learn-by-doing approach, creating a community of practice. USAID will also leverage in-house expertise and the knowledge within the ReMedios community to create learning spaces.The ReMedios activity contributes to RDO 2 and supports Pillar II of the RCS by strengthening independent media to track transnational corruption. It also advances Pillars III and V of the U.S. Strategy on Countering Corruption.</narrative>
  </description>
